\section{Experimental Setup and Evaluation Protocol}
\label{sec:experiment_design}

\subsection{Research Questions and Validation Hierarchy}

The evaluation was organized around five sequential research questions. RQ1 asked whether road-grade scheduling materially affects the frozen LPV-MPC closed loop. RQ2 asked whether ModernTCN-delta improves offline grade estimation relative to ModernTCN-22D, GRU-22D, and TCN-22D under a common data protocol. RQ3 asked whether the offline advantage transfers to closed-loop tracking and input regularity. RQ4 asked whether a qualified causal inertial observer provides complementary information and whether uncertainty-adaptive correction can exploit that information without replacing the learned estimate. RQ5 asked how the resulting Fusion-LPV-MPC compares with four fixed grade-source controls and what computational scope is supported by the measured timing evidence. This ordering separates the value of the scheduling variable from estimator selection, fusion behavior, and implementation timing.

No experiment was added for this manuscript rewrite. All values were read from frozen artifacts generated before the present reporting stage. The hierarchy distinguishes descriptive means, paired performance effects, qualification gates, and deployment claims. A favorable confidence interval for a performance metric was not treated as a pass for a separate safety or consistency gate.

\subsection{Simulation Platform and Frozen Controller Configuration}

All closed-loop cases used the same diagonal dual-drive-and-steer AGV plant revision, \texttt{agv\_physics\_v2\_plantfix}, and the same effective LPV-MPC entry point. The controller sample period was 0.01~s, the prediction horizon was 150 steps (1.5~s), and the control horizon was 30 steps (0.3~s). The effective state and input weights, input bounds, increment bounds, output bounds, soft-constraint weights, LPV database, and controller cache were frozen before the comparisons. Table~\ref{tab:frozen_experimental_configuration} reports the configuration that was actually executed rather than historical defaults.

