\subsection{Comparison Methods and Grade-Source Controls}

The estimator comparison used four methods: ModernTCN-delta, ModernTCN-22D, GRU-22D, and TCN-22D. The architecture-controlled comparison held the 22D input fixed for ModernTCN-22D, GRU-22D, and TCN-22D, whereas the representation ablation paired ModernTCN-delta with ModernTCN-22D. The controller-source comparison used zero-grade LPV-MPC, the simple causal-IMU baseline, MTCN-LPV-MPC, Fusion-LPV-MPC, and the truth-driven conditioned reference. The truth-driven conditioned reference is an analysis reference rather than a deployable estimator. Table~\ref{tab:comparison_protocol} specifies what changed and what remained fixed.

