\subsection{Closed-Loop Routes, Seeds, and Statistical Units}

The formal controller benchmark used six frozen routes: P1 factory logistics, P2 sharp-turn transition, P3 long uphill--downhill, P4 mild uphill/downhill with straight--turn coupling, P5 flat factory logistics, and P6 downhill recovery after a turn. The deterministic zero-grade, simple causal-IMU, and truth-driven sources contributed one case per route. Learned sources contributed ten model-seed cases per route. Consequently, deterministic contrasts were paired by route, whereas learned contrasts preserved the model-seed hierarchy before route aggregation. Figure~\ref{fig:closed_loop_route_set} fixes the six-route display contract.

