\subsection{RQ2: Does the Multi-Scale Delta Bank Improve Offline Grade Estimation?}

ModernTCN-delta achieved the lowest ten-seed mean grade MAE (0.59888$^{\circ}$) and registered $|\theta|\leq10^{\circ}$ P95 absolute error (1.67777$^{\circ}$) among the four estimators. Its paired MAE advantage was 0.05412$^{\circ}$ over ModernTCN-22D, 0.28694$^{\circ}$ over GRU-22D, and 0.31648$^{\circ}$ over TCN-22D, with every 95\% interval above zero. The representation-specific edge P95 improvement over ModernTCN-22D was 0.42608$^{\circ}$. Table~\ref{tab:estimator_and_delta_results} separates method means from paired effects so that architecture and representation claims are not conflated.

