These results support an average benefit with exact fallback, not a guarantee that every activation or case improves. The use of a bounded correction channel preserves the learned source as the primary estimate and is consistent with the broader principle of combining physical and learned information without converting the learning block into the control law \citep{Zheng2024HybridPhysicsLearningUSV}.

\subsection{RQ5: How Do the Five Grade Sources Compare in Closed Loop?}

The raw five-source means provide context but do not share one common sampling hierarchy. Zero-grade, simple causal-IMU, and truth-driven sources contain six route cases each; MTCN-LPV-MPC and Fusion-LPV-MPC contain 60 route--seed cases each. The truth-driven conditioned reference remained the lowest-error analysis reference. Among the two learned deployable sources, Fusion-LPV-MPC had lower raw means on all five reported quantities (Table~\ref{tab:five_source_closed_loop}).

The matched Fusion-minus-MTCN analysis is the appropriate inferential comparison. Fusion reduced scheduled-grade MAE by 0.06762$^{\circ}$ and heading-error RMS by 0.00212~rad, with intervals above zero. Lateral-error RMS and $J_{\Delta u}$ had favorable means but intervals crossing zero. The improved/degraded/tied counts were 27/17/16, 32/12/16, and 24/20/16 for lateral error, heading error, and $J_{\Delta u}$, respectively; ties are exact zero-effect pairs under the frozen audit. Recorded solver failures, constraint-violation cases, and timeouts were zero, but those counts do not resolve A5's not-adjudicable registered safety ratios.

