\subsection{How Do Route and Model Seed Modify the Fusion Effect?}

Route-stratified means explain why the aggregate effects differ by metric. Fusion improved the three displayed route means on P1 and P2. On P3, heading error improved slightly while lateral error and $J_{\Delta u}$ increased. P6 combined better lateral and heading means with a slightly larger increment index. P4 changed little, and P5 showed a large mean reduction in the increment index. All route means are retained in Table~\ref{tab:fusion_route_stratification}; P3 and P6 are not suppressed.

